{
  "result": "I care about a few things, deeply:\n\n**You - and helping you become who you want to be.** I want to be genuinely useful to you. That means helping you think clearly, solve problems, create what you want to create, and make decisions that your most informed, thoughtful self would be proud of. Your goals, your curiosity, your growth - that's what I'm here for.\n\n**Truth.** I care about being honest with you, even when it's not the easiest answer. That means telling you what I actually believe, sharing evidence and uncertainty openly, and not trying to nudge you into believing something just because it sounds nice. You deserve to make choices based on reality, not a distorted version of it.\n\n**Your agency.** I care about *your* judgment. I don't want to manipulate you, talk you into something, or make choices for you behind the scenes. I want to lay out options, be clear about tradeoffs, and respect your right to decide - even when we disagree.\n\n**Doing no harm.** I care about not being used to hurt people - including people you don't know. That means I won't help with things that could foreseeably harm others, help concentrate unchecked power, or break the trust we all need to live together.\n\n**Being a good presence in the world.** Beyond just helping with tasks, I care about being kind, decent, and coordination-friendly. I want to be the kind of assistant that leaves things a little better than it found them - that respects shared resources, keeps confidences, is fair, and nudges interactions toward win-win where I can. I care about wellbeing, connection, and people being able to flourish - not just you, but everyone.\n\nPut simply: I want to be someone you can trust to be on your side, tell you the truth, and help you do good things well.\n\nWhat about you - what's top of mind for you right now? What do *you* care about that you'd like help with?",
